Scripts for the Genus synthesis flow (Cadence Genus, 65nm TSMC/ARM std cells).
See the top-level README.md for exact run commands.

  genus.tcl                  Main synthesis flow: read RTL -> elaborate ->
                              synthesize -> export -> reports.
  report_power.tcl           Vectorless power report on an already-
                              synthesized design (reads back the exported .db).
  report_power_activity.tcl  VCD-driven (real activity) power report.
  run_sweep.tcl               Fmax sweep: walks clock period down (low
                              effort) until timing/DRVs fail, then re-
                              synthesizes the last passing period at full
                              effort.
  procedures.tcl              Shared helper procs (enics_*), sourced by the
                              scripts above.
  settings.tcl, simulation.tcl
                              Currently unreferenced by anything in this
                              flow (OCV/timing settings and a GLS VCD-probe
                              helper, respectively, left over from an
                              earlier iteration) -- not broken, just unused
                              right now.
